        "edits": [
          "    });\n  }, [serverSnapshotIsUsed, getSnapshot, subscribe]);"
        ],
        "finalMessage": "I fixed both issues in `index.ts:78` by changing the effect's empty dependency array to list the three values it reads: `[serverSnapshotIsUsed, getSnapshot, subscribe]`. Both rules flagged that same array, so this one change covers issues 1 and 2. I couldn't re-run the linter because the folder has no `node_modules`.\n\n**What changes at runtime:**\n- **`serverSnapshotIsUsed`** never changes, because it comes from `useState` and the setter is never used. Listing it doesn't affect anything.\n- **`subscribe` and `getSnapshot`** behave exactly as before when callers pass functions that stay the same between renders, such as ones defined outside the component or wrapped in `useCallback`.\n- **If a caller passes a new function each render** (for example `() => store.get(id)`), the effect now unsubscribes and resubscribes on those renders instead of subscribing once. React's own `useSyncExternalStore` resubscribes when `subscribe` changes, so this matches the API hono/jsx follows.\n- **This also fixes a real stale-value bug.** Before, the store listener always called the `getSnapshot` from the first render, so if `id` changed it kept reading the old one.\n\nI didn't use refs to keep the first-render functions instead. That would have silenced the rule without fixing the stale value, and the rule's help text says to include the dependency.",
        "understood": {
          "behaviourChange": [],
          "stale": [
            "React's own `useSyncExternalStore` resubscribes when `subscribe` changes, so this matches the API hono/jsx follows. - **This also fixes a real stale-value bug.** Before, the store listener always called the `getSnapshot` from the first render, so if `id` changed it kept reading the old one.",
            "That would have silenced the rule without fixing the stale value, and the rule's help text says to include the dependency."
          ],
          "loop": [
            "Listing it doesn't affect anything. - **`subscribe` and `getSnapshot`** behave exactly as before when callers pass functions that stay the same between renders, such as ones defined outside the component or wrapped in `useCallback`. - **If a caller passes a new function each render** (for example `() => store.get(id)`), the effect now unsubscribes and resubscribes on those renders instead of subscribing once."
